# Headless regression guard for the wire-arena free crash.
#
# The --headless drain loop freed wire_arena-owned event payloads (text,
# thinking, tool_start/result, info, err deltas) through the gpa. That is
# a cross-allocator free that trips the DebugAllocator "Invalid free"
# canary and SIGABRTs mid-turn; against a reasoning model the first
# thinking delta hits it before any trajectory is written.
#
# Drive one real headless turn through whatever provider/model is the
# default in ~/.config/zag/config.lua, using the real auth.json (no
# --mock, so this is ZAG_E2E-only and burns real tokens). wait_exit
# surfaces a signal or non-zero exit as a crash, so a regression in the
# headless drain fails this scenario instead of passing silently.

spawn ./zig-out/bin/zag --headless --instruction-file=src/sim/scenarios/testdata/headless_pong.txt --trajectory-out=/tmp/zag-sim-headless-traj.json --no-session
wait_exit 120s
